// ⭐⭐ **THE OP AS THE ARTIFACT KEEPS IT: every record in its payload the artifact's own.** A name, a label, a
// constant's bytes or a type in a payload is often a record the signature index holds, and an artifact built on a
// pool worker crosses back to the main thread while the worker keeps that index. So the artifact's doors copy what
// they store — this one for ops, the `record…` doors above, `IrFunction.create` and `VarInfo.make` — and a door of
// the index that hands a record out never does. An arm whose payload is scalars and value ids the parser built for
// this op holds nothing of the index's and is kept as it is.
function artifactOwnedOp(op MaxonOp) returns MaxonOp
